      "content": "While high protein is great for energy, some items like aged cheeses, salami, and soy sauce can be high in sodium and sometimes certain additives, which is something to monitor. Since you are on an MAOI, it's crucial to be very mindful of tyramine content, which these cured/aged foods often contain. Consider pairing those items with lots of fresh vegetables to boost your nutrition while staying safe. Always discuss your diet plan with your prescribing doctor or a nutritionist for personalized advice regarding medication interactions.",
